From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sydney <sydney@hyphen-emdash.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:08:07 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] Give sounds shorter than one block an empty range

chop_and_add sets a sound's end to the last block index. When the first
sound is shorter than one block there are no blocks yet, so its end
wrapped round to 4294967295 and searching read far past the blocks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 brain/src/brain.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/brain/src/brain.cpp b/brain/src/brain.cpp
index 4324148..3b31732 100644
--- a/brain/src/brain.cpp
+++ b/brain/src/brain.cpp
@@ -137,7 +137,8 @@ void brain::chop_and_add(sound &s, u32 count, u32 rate, bool ditchpcm) {
     }
     update_tick++;
   }
-  s.m_end = m_blocks.size()-1;
+  // a sound shorter than one block has no blocks at all
+  s.m_end = m_blocks.size()>s.m_start ? m_blocks.size()-1 : s.m_start;
   s.m_num_blocks = s.m_end-s.m_start;
 }
 
